From a3d7101724a4032497091111dee83edc64b231a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:50:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] HDR10+ as Dolby Vision: why not, once a
 video in kodi.log and in the player information

With "Play HDR10+ videos as Dolby Vision" on, an HDR10+ video is sent as
Dolby Vision only where the display takes native Dolby Vision in a mode
that carries it, the display is not sent HDR10+, and the video's output
is Automatic (Dolby Vision for the video forces it). Which of these
stopped it was said nowhere but in one debug line with an "or": a user
with the setting on saw nothing converted and nothing to say why.

Hdr10PlusAsDolbyVisionWhy() (DVPlaybackPolicy.h) gives the reason with
the same verdict: the setting off, another output chosen for the video,
no native Dolby Vision on this output (with the reason of the output),
or a display that takes HDR10+ and gets the video's own. The demuxer
asks once a stream, not for each picture; kodi.log says the reason once
a video at the info level, and the player information says it, with the
setting on, for an HDR10+ video that did not go out as Dolby Vision
(hdr10plus_not_dv): where the display takes HDR10+, with Dolby Vision
in "HDR output (this video)" as what to do; where there is no native
Dolby Vision, with the reason of the output, as for a Dolby Vision
video.

Strings 54958-54960 of Estuary in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx;
system/hades made again by make-playerinfo.py.
